---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Yugeng Zhou | Scientific Computing</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Yugeng Zhou: Scientific Computing, Mixed-Integer Optimization, and MIP Solver Engineering"
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,300;0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <aside class="sidebar" style={`background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(220,238,246,0.47), rgba(194,210,218,0.88)), url('${base}images/fulls/Welt.jpg')`}>
        <div class="sidebar-inner">
          <div class="avatar-shell" id="profile-avatar">
            <img
              src={`${base}images/avatar.jpg`}
              alt="Portrait of Yugeng Zhou"
              onerror="this.style.display='none'; this.parentElement.classList.add('no-image');"
            />
            <div class="avatar-fallback" aria-hidden="true">YZ</div>
          </div>

          <h1>Yugeng Zhou</h1>

          <p class="identity">
            Scientific Computing<br />
            Mixed-Integer Optimization<br />
            MIP Solver Engineering<br />
            Agentic Programming
          </p>

          <p class="small">Berlin, Germany</p>

          <nav class="sidebar-nav" aria-label="Section navigation">
            <a href="#about">About</a>
            <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
            <a href="#interests">Research Interests</a>
            <a href="#projects">Selected Projects</a>
            <a href="#education">Education</a>
          </nav>

          <div class="sidebar-links">
            <!-- Add public/cv.pdf to enable this link. -->
            <a href={`${base}cv.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CV</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/YugenixZ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              GitHub
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yugeng-zhou-yugenix/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              LinkedIn
            </a>
            <span>Email: yugengzhou[at]gmail[dot]com</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <main class="content">
        <section id="about" class="section">
          <h2>About</h2>
          <p>
            I am a Master's graduate in Scientific Computing from TU Berlin. My work focuses on
            mixed-integer optimization, optimization solver internals, and implementation-oriented computational research.
          </p>
          <p>
            I am particularly interested in the interaction between mathematical modeling decisions, optimization solver behavior, and computational performance, and in turning algorithmic ideas into experimentally grounded and verifiable implementations.
          </p>
          <p>
            “Your spark isn’t your purpose.”— Soul (2020)
          </p> 
        </section>

        <section id="experience" class="section">
          <h2>Experience</h2>

          <article class="entry">
            <h3>Algorithm Intern, Cardinal Operations (CO)</h3>
            <p class="meta">Mar. 2026 - Apr. 2026</p>
            <p>
              Built Python-based planning workflows for railway scheduling and resource assignment
              under complex operational constraints. Implemented batching and inheritance strategies
              to improve scalability on large instances, and designed structured experiments to
              evaluate runtime, solution quality, and trade-offs across alternative modeling and
              heuristic choices.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry">
            <h3>Research Assistant Intern, Zuse Institute Berlin (ZIB)</h3>
            <p class="meta">Nov. 2022 - Mar. 2023; Jan. 2024 - May. 2024</p>
            <p>
              Improved components of a parallel optimization solver and analyzed factors affecting
              runtime performance. Built visualization and evaluation scripts to better understand
              search behavior and solver dynamics, and benchmarked heuristic methods on standard
              instances to support performance-focused experimentation. I also developed
              optimization modeling and data transformation workflows for transportation-related
              planning tasks, including preprocessing and comparative experimental analysis across
              different data and model formats.
            </p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section id="interests" class="section">
          <h2>Research Interests</h2>
          <ul class="interest-list">
            <li>Mixed-integer programming</li>
            <li>Branch-and-bound and branching rules</li>
            <li>MIP Solver engineering</li>
            <li>Constraint recognition in MIP</li>
            <li>Computational optimization experiments</li>
            <li>Agentic Programming for optimization research workflows</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="projects" class="section">
          <h2>Selected Projects</h2>

          <!--
          <article class="entry">
            <h3>Agentic MIP Research: Accelerated Constraint Handler Generation </h3>
            <p class="meta">Python, PySCIPOpt, SCIP, MIP, LLM Agents</p>
            <p>
              Research-oriented workflow for Agentic Programming-assisted constraint recognition and solver-side plugin
              generation.
            </p>
          </article>
          -->

          <article class="entry">
            <h3>Branching on General Disjunctions using Distributed Memory Parallel Branch-and-Bound</h3>
            <p class="meta">C/C++, SCIP, FiberSCIP, Branch-and-Bound</p>
            <p>
              Master's thesis project implementing branching on general disjunctions in SCIP and
              extending it to FiberSCIP for parallel branch-and-bound evaluation.
            </p>
          </article>

        </section>

        <section id="education" class="section">
          <h2>Education</h2>

          <article class="entry compact">
            <h3>Technische Universitat Berlin</h3>
            <p class="meta">M.Sc. Scientific Computing, 2025</p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry compact">
            <h3>Harbin University of Science and Technology</h3>
            <p class="meta">B.Sc. Information and Computing Science, 2019</p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <footer class="footer">
          <p>© 2026 Yugeng Zhou</p>
          <p>Design adapted from HTML5 UP</p>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --page-bg: #ffffff;
    --sidebar-bg: #dceef6;
    --ink: #24363f;
    --muted: #5b707a;
    --line: #d4e3ea;
    --accent: #4f8299;
    --sidebar-width: 32%;
    --content-width: 860px;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #e8f5fb 0%, #f4fafd 30%, #ffffff 70%);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Source Serif 4", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, "Noto Serif", serif;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: #335f73;
  }

  .page {
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .sidebar {
    position: fixed;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: var(--sidebar-width);
    background-color: var(--sidebar-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    border-right: 1px solid #c6dce6;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }

  .sidebar-inner {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 34px 48px;
  }

  .avatar-shell {
    width: 136px;
    height: 136px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(58, 90, 105, 0.18);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    position: relative;
    background: #c4dce8;
  }

  .avatar-shell img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .avatar-fallback {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 1.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: #2d4b58;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .avatar-shell.no-image .avatar-fallback {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .sidebar h1 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 1.76rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .identity {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: #2e4753;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .small {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .sidebar-nav {
    margin: 22px 0;
    padding: 18px 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .sidebar-nav a {
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #365d70;
  }

  .sidebar-nav a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .sidebar-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px 14px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .content {
    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
    padding: 56px clamp(22px, 4vw, 52px) 44px;
    max-width: calc(var(--sidebar-width) + var(--content-width));
  }

  .section {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }

  .section + .section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 28px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 1.32rem;
    color: #233844;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    color: #203744;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .entry {
    padding: 15px 0 16px;
  }

  .entry + .entry {
    border-top: 1px solid #e2edf2;
  }

  .entry.compact {
    padding: 12px 0;
  }

  .meta {
    margin: 3px 0 9px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .interest-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 16px;
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    :root {
      --sidebar-width: 34%;
      --content-width: 760px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .sidebar {
      position: static;
      width: 100%;
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #c6dce6;
    }

    .sidebar-inner {
      max-width: 820px;
      padding: 28px 22px;
    }

    .content {
      margin-left: 0;
      max-width: 100%;
      padding: 26px 22px 34px;
    }

    .avatar-shell {
      width: 108px;
      height: 108px;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .sidebar h1 {
      font-size: 1.48rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    body {
      font-size: 15.5px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .sidebar-links {
      gap: 6px 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
